@divFloor(a, -b) * -b + @mod(a, -b) = a
If b divides a exactly, we have @divFloor(a, -b) * -b = a
Else, we have @divFloor(a, -b) * -b > a, so @mod(a, -b) becomes negative

@divFloor(-a, b) * b + @mod(-a, b) = a
If b divides a exactly, we have @divFloor(-a, b) * b = -a
Else, we have @divFloor(-a, b) * b < -a, so @mod(-a, b) becomes positive

